<title>ITALY: ITALY BONDS/BTPS START FIRMER WITH OTHER DEBT MKTS.</title>
<headline>ITALY BONDS/BTPS START FIRMER WITH OTHER DEBT MKTS.</headline>
<text>
<p>0720 GMT - Italian bonds and Btp futures started firmer, buoyed by Bunds and U.S. Treasuries, in a thin holiday market eyeing raft of U.S. data later today particularly July CPI. Italian MTS secondary government bond market closes at midday ahead of Assumption holiday Friday while MIF futures market closed both Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>* Bonds:Jul07 +23bps at 101.26, yield 6.67, Bund spread 100bps</p>
<p>* Futures:SepLIF +35bps at 135.58. Res 135.87, sup 135.50</p>
<p>* Lira:steady vs mark at 977.70/7.90</p>
<p>(FULL BACKGROUND / DETAILS FOLLOW)</p>
